# Non-Equilibrium & Information Thermodynamics
#
# Onsager reciprocity, Prigogine dissipative structures, Jarzynski equality, and Landauer erasure limits.

#>spw_cache_univ_thermo_nonequilibrium
#:cache #!thermodynamics
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model advanced graduate curricula in non-equilibrium thermodynamics, stochastic fluctuation theorems, biophysical dissipation, and information thermodynamics."
  ~#frontiers: "Far-from-equilibrium self-organization, single-molecule work relations, Landauer erasure, and black hole horizon entropy"
}

^["linear_non_equilibrium_thermodynamics_and_onsager"]{
  flux_force_formalism: "Macroscopic transport driven by thermodynamic potential gradients near equilibrium."
  phenomenological_laws: #[
    "Forces & Conjugate Fluxes: Thermodynamic driving forces X_i (grad 1/T, -grad mu/T) and resultant fluxes J_i (heat, mass, electric current)",
    "Entropy Production Rate: sigma = Sum(J_i * X_i) >= 0; local Second Law formulation of continuous dissipation",
    "Onsager Reciprocal Relations: Symmetry of cross-phenomenological coefficients L_ik = L_ki derived from microscopic time-reversal invariance",
    "Coupled Transport Effects: Thermoelectric phenomena (Seebeck voltage, Peltier cooling), thermodiffusion (Soret effect), and diffusion-thermo (Dufour effect)"
  ]
}

^["far_from_equilibrium_dissipative_structures"]{
  self_organization: "Nonlinear thermodynamic systems far from equilibrium birthing spontaneous spatial and temporal order (Prigogine paradigm)."
  nonlinear_phenomena: .{
    bifurcations_and_oscillations: #[
      "Prigogine Minimum Entropy Production Theorem: Valid only in linear regime; unstable far from equilibrium",
      "Chemical Oscillators: Belousov-Zhabotinsky (BZ) reaction, limit cycles, and concentration wave fronts",
      "Reaction-Diffusion Morphogenesis: Alan Turing instability forming biological spots, stripes, and skeletal patterns"
    ]
    hydrodynamic_instabilities: "Rayleigh-Benard thermal convection rolls and Taylor-Couette vortex formation when Rayleigh or Taylor numbers cross critical thresholds"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["stochastic_thermodynamics_and_fluctuation_theorems"]{
  nanoscale_energetics: "Thermodynamics of small, fluctuating systems (colloids, single biomolecules, molecular motors)."
  fluctuation_theorems: #[
    "Jarzynski Equality: <exp(-W / k_B*T)> = exp(-Delta_F / k_B*T), extracting exact equilibrium free energy differences from irreversible non-equilibrium work measurements",
    "Crooks Fluctuation Theorem: Exact ratio of forward work probability P(W) to time-reversed work probability P_R(-W) equals exp((W - Delta_F) / k_B*T)",
    "Single-Molecule Optical Tweezers: Pulling RNA/DNA hairpins to measure mechanical folding landscapes through stochastic work trajectories"
  ]
}

^["information_thermodynamics_and_maxwell_demons"]{
  information_energy_equivalence: "The physical reality of information and the thermodynamic cost of computation."
  information_laws: .{
    maxwell_demon_resolution: "Information acquisition requires measurement; the Demon must store bits, and erasing that memory generates entropy that saves the Second Law"
    szilard_single_molecule_engine: "Extracting exactly k_B * T * ln(2) of work from a thermal bath by measuring which half of a box contains a single particle"
    landauer_erasure_principle: "The erasure of one bit of logical information inevitably dissipates at least k_B * T * ln(2) of heat into the environment"
    sagawa_ueda_generalized_second_law: "Work extraction bound <W_ext> <= -Delta_F + k_B*T * I, where I is the mutual information acquired by feedback measurement"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["biophysical_bioenergetics_and_gravitational_entropy"]{
  extremes_of_dissipation: #[
    "Mitchell Chemiosmotic Coupling: Proton-motive force across mitochondrial membranes driving ATP synthase rotary motors at near 100% thermodynamic efficiency",
    "Hopfield Kinetic Proofreading: Non-equilibrium ATP dissipation driving high-fidelity DNA replication and translation far beyond thermal equilibrium limits",
    "Bekenstein-Hawking Black Hole Entropy: Horizon entropy S_BH = (k_B * c^3 * A) / (4 * G * hbar), showing that maximum entropy scales with surface area rather than volume (Holographic Principle)"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Non-equilibrium thermodynamics reveals that life is not a defiance of the Second Law, but its most exquisite instrument: a swirling whirlpool dissipating solar energy into exquisite order."
  ~#wonder: "Why does the erasure of a single abstract bit of data on a computer chip have a mandatory, non-negotiable physical cost in micro-joules of heat?"

  principles: #[
    "Information is physical: A bit cannot exist without a physical carrier; erasing bits dumps entropy into the heat bath.",
    "Order requires continuous dissipation: To maintain a living cell against thermal decay, energy must continuously flow through and dissipate.",
    "Fluctuations contain the equilibrium: Even when driving a system violently out of equilibrium, the Jarzynski relation proves that the equilibrium free energy is secretly encoded in the distribution of failures."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Entropy production rate density (sigma) must be strictly non-negative at every spatial point in continuous media.",
  "Calculations of computational energy consumption must respect the Landauer erasure limit (E_erase >= k_B * T * ln 2 per bit).",
  "Experimental verification of fluctuation theorems must account for instrumental drift and finite trap stiffness.",
}

#>wonder_thermo_nonequilibrium_1
?["Can reversible computing architectures operate below the Landauer thermodynamic limit at room temperature?"]{
  #:depth #!physical ~#lens(reversible_computation)
  ~#hypothesis: "Adiabatic and ballistic superconducting flux quantum computing circuits can execute logical operations with dissipation levels three orders of magnitude below k_B*T*ln(2) by avoiding logical bit erasure through fully bijective unitary information pipelines."
  !probe{ "Measure cryogenic microwatt thermal dissipation per clock cycle in reversible adiabatic CMOS vs standard irreversible logic gates." }
  $%[computation.energy_dissipation_per_cycle_joules, physics.landauer_bound_ratio]
}
